📩 [Inquire About Consulting Services](mailto:david@daexai.com?subject=n8n%20Consultation%20Request)", "height": 580, "width": 400}, "position": [-660, -260], "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "eadab384-f0d6-48b1-b4dd-e0eb106228ac", "name": "Sticky Note1", "parameters": {"color": 7, "content": "## 📊 Sample Data

This node creates sample user data with intentional duplicates based on email addresses.

**What it does:**
- Creates an array of users
- Includes duplicate entries (same email)
- Simulates real-world messy data

**Next Step:** Pass this data to the deduplication code node", "height": 360, "width": 300}, "position": [-240, 220], "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "745ba692-ffa8-4ac6-851f-fb9dde8392f2", "name": "Sticky Note2", "parameters": {"color": 7, "content": "## 🧹 Deduplication Logic

**Key Concepts:**
- `filter()` - Creates new array with filtered elements
- `findIndex()` - Returns index of first matching element
- `index === self.findIndex()` - Keeps only first occurrence

**Algorithm:**
1. Parse JSON data
2. Filter array keeping first occurrence of each email
3. Transform back to n8n format
4. Return deduplicated results", "height": 380, "width": 300}, "position": [100, 220], "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "8bc4bd06-b031-4909-8210-5ec1f11366ff", "name": "Sticky Note3", "parameters": {"color": 7, "content": "## 📈 Results

**What you'll see:**
- Original count: 6 items
- Deduplicated count: 4 items
- Duplicates removed: 2 items

**Use Cases:**
- Clean data before CRM import
- Prevent duplicate database entries
- Data quality improvement
- ETL pipeline cleanup", "height": 380, "width": 300}, "position": [460, 220], "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "typeVersion": 1}, {"id": "75a624be-73e9-4b35-ae58-33bc45a0208c", "name": "Create Sample Data", "parameters": {"jsCode": "// Create sample data with intentional duplicates
const usersWithDuplicates = [
  { id: 1, name: "John Doe", email: "john@example.com", department: "Engineering" },
  { id: 2, name: "Jane Smith", email: "jane@example.com", department: "Marketing" },
  { id: 3, name: "John Doe", email: "john@example.com", department: "Engineering" }, // Duplicate
  { id: 4, name: "Bob Johnson", email: "bob@example.com", department: "Sales" },
  { id: 5, name: "Alice Brown", email: "alice@example.com", department: "HR" },
  { id: 6, name: "Jane Smith Updated", email: "jane@example.com", department: "Marketing" } // Duplicate
];

// Return the sample data as a single item with usersJson property
return [{
  json: {
    usersJson: JSON.stringify(usersWithDuplicates),
    totalCount: usersWithDuplicates.length,
    message: "Sample data with duplicates created"
  }
}];"}, "position": [-200, 80], "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "909634f2-52ad-4f98-aad0-7c3d8a8b8e43", "name": "Deduplicate Users", "parameters": {"jsCode": "// 🧱 Data Deduplication Code Node
// Use Case: Clean up duplicates before inserting into DB or CRM

// Parse the users JSON from the previous node
const users = JSON.parse(items[0].json.usersJson);

// Deduplicate users based on email address
// This keeps the first occurrence of each unique email
const uniqueUsers = users.filter(
  (user, index, self) => 
    index === self.findIndex(u => u.email === user.email)
);

// Log the deduplication results
console.log(`Original count: ${users.length}`);
console.log(`Deduplicated count: ${uniqueUsers.length}`);
console.log(`Duplicates removed: ${users.length - uniqueUsers.length}`);

// Return the deduplicated users in n8n format
// Each user becomes a separate item in the workflow
return uniqueUsers.map(user => ({ json: user }));"}, "position": [140, 80], "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "59855549-51e4-42df-b586-730ff1e59e67", "name": "Display Results", "parameters": {"jsCode": "// Display the final results with statistics
const currentItems = items;
const uniqueCount = currentItems.length;

// Create a summary of the deduplication process
const summary = {
  deduplicated_users: currentItems.map(item => item.json),
  statistics: {
    unique_users_count: uniqueCount,
    process_completed: true,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
  },
  message: `Successfully deduplicated data - ${uniqueCount} unique users remaining`
};

return [{ json: summary }];"}, "position": [500, 80], "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code", "typeVersion": 2}, {"id": "2a5c40fc-ff56-4e54-b06e-4c56e2c4da0e", "name": "Sticky Note4", "parameters": {"color": 7, "content": "## 🎯 Learning Objectives

**After this tutorial you'll understand:**

✅ How to use JavaScript array methods in n8n
✅ Data deduplication techniques
✅ Working with JSON data in Code nodes
✅ Transforming data between n8n items
✅ Practical use cases for data cleaning

**Best Practices:**
- Always validate input data
- Consider performance for large datasets
- Test with various duplicate scenarios
- Add error handling for production use", "height": 330, "width": 430}, "position": [-140, -240], "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "typeVersion": 1}], "pinData": {}, "settings": {"executionOrder": "v1"}, "tags": [], "versionId": "03170dda-ff22-468b-be1c-e32424a27c66"}

